.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-SETUP 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-setup
.Nd install and configure what a machine needs to be a Kubernetes node, online or from the darksite
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
makes this machine ready for
.Xr kube-init 8
or
.Xr kube-join 8 ,
on dnf systems (CentOS, RHEL, Rocky, Fedora) and apt systems (Debian,
Ubuntu).
In order it:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
when
.Ev KLDLOAD_DARKSITE_URL
is set, copies the version lock, charts, manifests, command-line tools and
container images from the host's darksite, and installs every package
from its mirror only;
.It
sets the node's time source and its routes to the cluster;
.It
installs the QEMU guest agent;
.It
loads the kernel modules and sysctls Kubernetes needs, and turns swap
off;
.It
installs containerd, with the systemd cgroup driver, and kubeadm,
kubelet, kubectl and cri-tools from
.Ql pkgs.k8s.io
or the darksite;
.It
installs Helm, the Cilium CLI, Hubble and k9s: the darksite's copy when
there is one, otherwise downloaded and checked against the SHA-256 each
release publishes;
.It
installs node_exporter;
.It
loads the darksite's container images, pulls any image the lock or
kubeadm names that is still missing, and counts what came from where;
.It
sets up networking for clones: DHCP with a client id from the MAC,
unless NetworkManager owns the interface.
.El
.Pp
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description and environment and exit 0, without root.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev K8S_VERSION
The package stream, as a minor version:
.Ql v1.37 .
From the caller, else
.Pa /root/darksite/k8s-stack.lock ,
else
.Ql dl.k8s.io Ns 's
current release; if none answers, it stops.
.It Ev HELM_VERSION , Ev CILIUM_CLI_VERSION , Ev HUBBLE_CLI_VERSION
Each tool's release: from the caller, else the lock; a lock without one
is refused.
With no lock at all each is GitHub's latest release.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_DARKSITE_URL
The host's darksite as
.Xr kube-cluster 8
tunnels it into a golden, e.g.
.Ql http://127.0.0.1:18080 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/darksite/k8s-stack.lock
The versions the image was built with.
.It Pa /root/darksite/bin/
Command-line tool archives baked into the image; Helm's, the Cilium
CLI's, Hubble's and k9s's are checked against their sums when baked.
.It Pa /root/darksite/k8s-images/
Container images, loaded by
.Xr kube-load-images 8 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, named.
A required tool that does not download and verify is a failure; Hubble
and k9s are warned about.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The download steps alone, run in a Fedora 44 container with no darksite,
at the lock's versions:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[kube-setup] Installing Helm v4.3.0...
[kube-setup] Helm installed: v4.3.0+gbec5b06
[kube-setup] Installing Cilium CLI v0.20.1...
[kube-setup] Cilium CLI installed
[kube-setup] Installing Hubble CLI v1.19.4...
[kube-setup] Hubble CLI installed
[kube-setup] Installing k9s...
[kube-setup] k9s installed
.Ed
.Pp
The check itself, given Helm's archive and Cilium's list of sums, which
has no line for it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[kube-setup] helm-v4.3.0-linux-amd64.tar.gz: the release publishes sha256 'none', the download is 86584a54def73570558f66f5111cc53dfed56689637ae32c1201205d494f54fb
.Ed
.Pp
The archive was removed and nothing installed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr kube-init 8 ,
.Xr kube-join 8 ,
.Xr kube-load-images 8 ,
.Xr kube-smoke-test 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-27 a golden built "offline" was found fetching containerd,
kubeadm, Helm and every image from the internet; since then everything
comes from the host's darksite when it is given.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: downloaded tools were piped into
.Xr tar 1
as root without a check.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It disables swap, including zram, for good: the kubelet refuses to run
with it.
.Pp
Without
.Ev KLDLOAD_DARKSITE_URL
it adds the Kubernetes, and on some systems Docker and ZFS, package
repositories to the machine.
